Round 13 (2026-02-27)

What landed
- Files changed:
  - `clang/aot/emit.c`
  - `clang/aot/_.c`
- Introduced lazy lexical-environment materialization for emitted AOT code:
  - Each compiled function now allocates local arrays:
    - `Term env_cells[AOT_ENV_CAP]`
    - `u64 env_locs[AOT_ENV_CAP]`
  - Head/expr LAM binders no longer eagerly do `heap_alloc(2)` for env cells.
    - They store substitution payload in `env_cells[idx]` and keep `env_locs[idx]=0`.
  - Added runtime helpers in `clang/aot/_.c`:
    - `aot_env_head(env_cells, env_locs, len)`
    - `aot_env_get(env_cells, env_locs, idx)`
  - Fallback ALO emission now passes `aot_env_head(...)` instead of direct `e{dep-1}` vars.
  - DP expression emission (`DP0/DP1`) now uses `aot_env_get(...)` to obtain binder locations.
- Added lazy link wiring for DUP-backed env cells:
  - DUP cells are emitted with link `0` initially.
  - `aot_env_head` now patches existing cell links to the proper previous location when materializing a prefix.

Why
- Target was to cut per-interaction heap traffic from eager env-cell allocation on lambda binders.
- This is a correctness-preserving step toward stack/local-first case-tree execution, while keeping deopt ALO reconstruction valid.

